From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yaozhi mpv build <build@local.invalid>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 09:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] audio: allow 10- and 12-channel spatial output

SDL2 rejects every requested audio layout above eight channels in the
public prepare_audiospec() path, before the Windows WASAPI backend can
apply its WAVEFORMATEXTENSIBLE speaker mask.  This makes the dedicated
5.1.4 and 7.1.4 WASAPI support unreachable and reports:

    Unsupported number of audio channels.

Keep the existing safety limit for all other non-standard counts, but
allow the two spatial layouts supported by the bundled backend:

10ch: FL FR FC LFE SL SR TFL TFR TBL TBR
12ch: FL FR FC LFE BL BR SL SR TFL TFR TBL TBR
---
 src/audio/SDL_audio.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audio/SDL_audio.c b/src/audio/SDL_audio.c
index 421adbc..baa6fad 100644
--- a/src/audio/SDL_audio.c
+++ b/src/audio/SDL_audio.c
@@ -1284,7 +1284,8 @@ static int prepare_audiospec(const SDL_AudioSpec *orig, SDL_AudioSpec *prepared)
         } else {
             prepared->channels = 2;
         }
-    } else if (orig->channels > 8) {
+    } else if (orig->channels > 8 && orig->channels != 10 &&
+               orig->channels != 12) {
         SDL_SetError("Unsupported number of audio channels.");
         return 0;
     }
